            },
            {
              "id": "1c428d70-7d1f-44f2-b65f-991cd4bd0aaf",
              "name": "scoring_prompt",
              "value": "=Score how relevant this research paper is to an applied AI engineer interested in:\n\n* LLM agents and agentic workflows\n* RAG, retrieval, embeddings, and vector databases\n* LLM evaluation, testing, reliability, and observability\n* Tool use, memory, orchestration, and MCP\n* Production AI systems, latency, cost, and quality\n* Practical AI automation\n\nPaper title: {{ $json.title }}\nAbstract: {{ $json.summary }}\n\nReturn exactly one overall relevance score as an integer from 0 through 10 inclusive.\n\nThe score MUST NOT be below 0 or above 10. Do not add or total multiple scores.\n\nReturn only:\n{\"score\": 0, \"reason\": \"One concise explanation.\"}\n\nGive high scores only when the paper offers knowledge that could realistically improve the design, evaluation, or operation of applied LLM systems. A paper merely using AI in a specialized domain is not automatically relevant.\n\nFor scores of 7 or higher, prioritize work that directly changes how an applied engineer should design, evaluate, validate, or operate an LLM system. This can include theoretical work when it exposes a concrete failure mode or invalid assumption in production evaluation, calibration, safety, or reliability. Do not give 7+ merely because a paper involves LLM reasoning, memory, retrieval, agents, or latency; research on model-internal reasoning techniques, training methods, or benchmark improvements should remain below 7 unless the contribution transfers clearly to application-layer systems built with existing models.",
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "id": "418948f8-6f43-4e47-827c-0e034be2313c",
              "name": "input_price_per_million_usd",
              "value": 3,
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "id": "e0f53d6b-366f-492a-94db-30bcec33e32a",
              "name": "output_price_per_million_usd",
